, "is_card_required": false, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 8500, "description": "## Duration, Distance, Terrain\n1.5 hours\n1 mile at a moderate pace, stopping at various sites along the tour\nMostly flat surfaces and little to no inclines\n## About\n\"My Eyes are so diverted with Chimney Sweeps, Carriers of Wood, Merchants, Ladies, Priests, Carts, Horses, Oxen, Coaches, Market men and Women, Soldiers, Sailors, and my Ears with the Rattle Gabble of them all...\" -- John Adams, diary, March 18-19, 1759\n\nFollow the words and history of four generations of Adamses, from their experiences at the Old State House, through Beacon Hill, and into Back Bay. John, Abigail, and their descendants were prolific writers. The trove of documents they left behind intimately describe their lives, public service, and Boston from the eve of the Revolution to the turn of the twentieth century.\n## Meeting location:\nMeet your guide at the Boston Massacre Marker in front of the Old State House\n\nFinding Your Guide: All guides carry an 8×11 sign that says “Boston By Foot Walking Tours.”\n\nNearest Accessible MBTA Station: State Street (Orange line)\n## What to bring\nComfortable shoes, dress for the weather, water bottle", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "", "booking_notes": "", "cancellation_notes": "", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "Follow the words and history of the Adams Family over four generations", "short_description": null, "image_url": "", "image_cdn_url": "", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonbyfoot/items/455619/images/1335878/", "pk": 1335878, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/qMX7uYUSTWcc2WH4sjR0", "image_cdn_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/qMX7uYUSTWcc2WH4sjR0", "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonby